        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Story of the Man Who Turned into a Dog, Historias\n- Concepts: Theatre of the Absurd, Metatheatre, Magic realism\n- Topics: absurdist fiction, post–World War II theatre\n\nFacts:\n- Theatre of the Absurd is a post–World War II designation for particular plays of absurdist fiction written by primarily European playwrights in the late 1950s.\n- Theatre of the Absurd also names the style of theatre that evolved from those plays.\n- The Story of the Man Who Turned into a Dog can be classified as Theatre of the Absurd.\n- The Story of the Man Who Turned into a Dog and the other Historias can also be classified as Metatheatre and Magic realism.",
